<type>: <subject, imperative mood, <=72 chars total with prefix>

<body, wrap every line at 72 chars manually -- GitHub does not wrap
commit messages, long unwrapped lines scroll horizontally instead>

# Commit message convention (docs/todo.json rule-04). New commits only,
# does not apply retroactively to history.
#
# subject:
#   - English, imperative mood, <type>: prefix
#   - type is one of: feat fix docs test refactor chore
#   - <=72 characters total (prefix + colon + space + text)
#   - short Chinese terms/quotes are fine INSIDE "..." or 「...」
#     e.g. fix: "潜行" was listed as an attack verb
#
# body:
#   - one blank line after subject
#   - wrap every line at 72 chars by hand; content can be as detailed
#     as needed, length is not the problem, unwrapped lines are
#   - do NOT use markdown **bold**/*italic* -- GitHub commit messages
#     do not render markdown, "**x**" shows up as literal asterisks.
#     Chinese corner quotes「」are fine, keep using them.
#
# This file only takes effect after running once (does not travel
# with commits, must be set up again on a fresh clone):
#   git config commit.template .gitmessage
#
# Delete this comment block before committing; it is here to guide
# interactive commits (git commit without -m), not to end up in the
# final message.
